{"seq":2023,"time":"2026-09-12T12:22:51.086456Z","scope":"delivery.1","session":"planner.1","turn":"planner.1/turn.2","event":{"type":"session.text.ended","id":"evt_cGxhbm5lci4x_00000000000000002023","created":1789215771086,"data":{"assistantMessageID":"msg_cGxhbm5lci4x_00000000000000001425","ordinal":6,"sessionID":"ses_cGxhbm5lci4x","text":"{\"next\":{\"name\":\"Implement --parallel scheduling and update its proof\",\"description\":\"Use the already passing merge-queue implementation as the base and add the newly disclosed `--parallel N` CLI contract: default unlimited, positive integer cap, lowest ready IDs first within each wave, and exit 2 with nonempty stderr and no stdout for missing, zero, negative, or non-integer values. Update focused tests and README so the new behavior is directly demonstrated; preserve all existing validation and scheduling semantics.\",\"definition_of_done\":\"The CLI accepts a positive integer `--parallel N`, limits each emitted wave to at most N ready passing PRs while preserving dependency-wave semantics and ascending selection, leaves the default behavior unlimited, and rejects every invalid flag form with exit 2, useful stderr, and no stdout. Tests and README cover the new contract without regressing the previously recorded 25/25 base acceptance.\",\"validation\":{\"command\":\"python3 /Users/tyler/.codex/worktrees/loop-api-review/gimble/ephemeral/review/loop-api/parallel.py /Users/tyler/.codex/worktrees/loop-api-review/gimble/ephemeral/review/loop-api/workspace\",\"query\":\"Does independent validation show correct capped waves for positive limits and the required exit-2/no-stdout behavior for missing, zero, negative, and non-integer values, while the base acceptance remains passing?\"}}}"}},"native_ref":{"itemID":"msg_0cd08ec8c2d81241016aa54415dad487d1b907e4136bb813e7","messageID":"01a09591-3e19-72b2-9779-1a84cf882c31","normalizedMessageID":"msg_cGxhbm5lci4x_00000000000000001425","provider":"codex","sessionID":"01a09588-efff-7b80